Error [jet.ViewOutlivesOwner]: This view points into `xs`, which this function owns
  --> returned_view_bare_local_place_outlives_owner.jet:5:5
    |
  5 |     xs
    |     ^^
 Why: `xs` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305
